vine 1.2.0
prefix: mx
title: Localmodal model catalog expansion
---
[mx] Extend localmodal beyond Qwen (planning)
Add one additional model family to the developer tool without adding a second model-selection ceremony or independent lifecycle. The model family is selected only after compatibility and operating-cost evidence exists.
-> mx/canary
> One active Modal deployment remains the lifecycle boundary; selecting another catalog entry reconciles that deployment to the selected model.
> No model family is a product commitment until the discovery task records its Hub identity, revision, license/access conditions, vLLM compatibility, and measured resource regime.
> Model families extend the single LocalmodalRuntime through typed definitions and adapters; no provider or MCP transport may create another runtime, controller, credential cache, request builder, or stream parser.
---
[mx/discovery] Select the next model family from evidence (notstarted)
Research candidate families against the current OpenAI-compatible vLLM path and the developer-tool constraints. Record one candidate model ID and revision, license/access requirements, context and GPU requirements, parser/template needs, and reasons adjacent candidates were deferred.
Accept: one candidate is named with source links and a bounded compatibility hypothesis; no second family is added in the same pass.
---
[mx/authoring] Define the model authoring contract (notstarted)
Extend the model definition boundary so a new model can declare identity, profiles, capabilities, and a typed runtime-adapter selection without editing lifecycle orchestration, Copilot transport, or MCP transport.
Accept: adding a model that fits an existing adapter requires a model definition and catalog registration only; every adapter executes inside the single LocalmodalRuntime; unsupported behavior is rejected by the type boundary or an explicit adapter error.
-> mx/discovery
-> mx/foundation
---
[mx/adapter] Extract the typed runtime adapter boundary (notstarted)
Move Qwen-specific deployment flags and request/template behavior behind a typed adapter selected by the shared LocalmodalRuntime. Preserve current Qwen behavior and keep one common OpenAI-compatible streaming implementation.
Accept: Qwen behavior is unchanged, a second adapter can own family-specific options without conditionals spread through transports, and no adapter introduces another controller, credential store, request loop, or stream parser.
-> mx/authoring
---
[mx/catalog] Register a multi-model production catalog (notstarted)
Replace the single-model construction with an explicit production catalog and a declared default. Keep one active deployment and preserve the existing Copilot model-picker contract.
Accept: all catalog entries are presented through the same provider path, the default remains explicit, and no deployment choice becomes a new workspace setting.
-> mx/adapter
-> mx/authoring
---
[mx/deployment] Reconcile one active deployment across models (notstarted)
Define how endpoint state, Modal app identity, cache identity, and stop/start behavior change when the selected model changes. Keep model switching explicit and avoid silently serving a different model from saved endpoint state.
Accept: a model switch cannot reuse an endpoint or cache for the wrong model, and lifecycle tests cover start, switch, readiness, and stop with one active deployment.
-> mx/catalog
---
[mx/contracts] Prove the authoring and adapter seams (notstarted)
Add contract tests for model definitions, adapter selection, catalog presentation, deployment-spec translation, runtime request options, and the one-deployment model-switch policy.
Accept: fixture models exercise the same single runtime as production models, unsupported capabilities fail at a named boundary, and Copilot/MCP transport tests remain model-agnostic.
-> mx/adapter
-> mx/authoring
-> mx/catalog
-> mx/deployment
---
[mx/canary] Witness one additional family end to end (notstarted)
Implement the selected canary model through the authoring contract, run ordinary fixture/Extension Host tests, then run one opt-in Modal deployment and inference witness at a declared context profile.
Accept: the canary appears in the Copilot picker, uses the shared provider and delegation MCP path, completes a real streamed request through Modal, and records timing/cost conditions; the result determines whether the family expands further.
-> mx/contracts
-> mx/discovery
---
ref [mx/foundation] Validated single-runtime localmodal foundation (localmodal.vine)
The initial extension path, including its single runtime authority and end-to-end witness, must be complete before model authoring begins.
